// ugui/idl/builder.{h,cc}: builds a widget tree from a parsed .ugui document
// (idl::parser's AST): element types to widget constructors, properties to
// styles, classes, state overrides and transitions, @keyframes, @media
// (re-resolved on viewport changes), components with props and slots, CSS
// variables. Imports are merged by the parser.
//
// Shape differences (not behavior):
//
// * No active registry: build, rebuild, apply_style_class and
//   reapply_media_queries take the World first. build and rebuild also take
//   the WidgetContext the setters that change widget state need
//   (set_checked, set_radio_selected, set_toggle_on); a widget being built
//   has no context yet, so those calls behave as on a detached widget, as in
//   the C++.
// * No `set_animator`: the builder keeps no view of UIContext's animator.
//   @keyframes start on `ctx.animator`; a context without one (none) is the
//   C++ builder without an animator, which skips them.
// * WidgetFactory is `own fn(&var World, String): WidgetId` (the C++
//   `Function<wid(const String& name)>` plus the World it reached through
//   the active registry; the name is an owned copy, see PORTING.md pitfalls).
// * The C++ dispatch tables (kPropertyTable, kStyleMaskTable and the enum
//   lookups) are if-chains over the same names in the same order. The C++
//   resolves a value (`--var`) only for a known property; resolving is pure,
//   so here every value is resolved and an unknown key is then ignored.
// * MediaStyle::Query is MediaStyleQuery; MediaStyle is a component with the
//   key kMediaStyle.

module ultragui::idl::builder;

